# Source of truth for the protobuf-5 all-features CI lock: the light tier with [stac] and [vizx],
# at the versions the env5 runtime family (Serverless env 5 / classic DBR 17.3–18) preinstalls.
# (On Databricks those runtimes install the env5 wheel; this lock tests the plain wheel's light
# tier off Databricks with the same versions.)
#
# Regenerate (from python/geobrix/):
#   uv pip compile --generate-hashes --python-version 3.12 \
#       --output-file requirements-light-env5-all-ci.txt requirements-light-env5-all-ci.in
#
# This .in uses a local-package-with-extras reference so uv expands the base dependencies and
# [stac] + [vizx] directly from pyproject.toml; the holds below are the env5 runtimes' versions.
# ([overture] is opt-in and left out.) Protobuf-6 all-features twin: requirements-light-env6-all-ci.in.
#
# Note: CI resolves without Serverless grpcio-status constraints; the protobuf version
# in this lock (5.x) reflects the mapbox-vector-tile<2.2 hold below, NOT a CI
# grpcio constraint. The real runtime protobuf is set at cluster install time.

# Local package — the base dependencies plus [stac] and [vizx] from pyproject.toml
.[stac,vizx]

# The env5 runtimes' preinstalled versions (DBR 17.3 / 18, Serverless env 5): pandas 2.2.3,
# numpy 2.1.3, urllib3 2.3.0, click 8.1.7-8.1.8, protobuf 5 (mapbox-vector-tile 2.2 needs 6).
# The plain wheel has floors only; these holds keep the lock at the runtime family's versions.
pandas<2.3
numpy<2.2
urllib3<2.4
click<8.2
mapbox-vector-tile>=2.1,<2.2
rio-tiler>=9.0,<10

# pyspark is NOT a geobrix base dependency (Databricks provides it on every supported
# runtime; see pyproject.toml). This lock is for local/manual verification off-cluster,
# so pin it explicitly — same floor the base dependency used to carry.
pyspark>=4.0.0

# pillow is resolved through [vizx] (matplotlib, scikit-image, imageio, contextily) and certifi
# through requests and httpx2; the floors keep a regenerated lock at the security-patched
# releases. CI-only: the extras in pyproject.toml are unchanged, and pip leaves the runtime's own
# pillow and certifi in place.
pillow>=13.0.0
certifi>=2026.10.19
